And before you ask,


00:17:04.302 --> 00:17:06.174
I handcuffed myself
for tactical reasons


00:17:06.348 --> 00:17:08.089
that I do not have time
to explain.


00:17:08.263 --> 00:17:10.134
You shouldn'’t have gone off
on your own.


00:17:10.308 --> 00:17:12.006
We'’re supposed to be a team.


00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:14.399
Sorry, buddy.
I'’m still working on this teamwork thing.


00:17:14.573 --> 00:17:16.097
So now what?


00:17:16.271 --> 00:17:18.447
Well, I'’m not jumping
out of any more helicopters


00:17:18.621 --> 00:17:20.623
until we get some answers
from GUN.


00:17:20.797 --> 00:17:22.364
We need somewhere to regroup.


00:17:23.887 --> 00:17:25.715
I know just the place.


00:17:25.889 --> 00:17:28.283
["Lollipop"
by TEMPURA KIDZ playing]


00:17:33.897 --> 00:17:35.464
[all clapping]


00:17:36.247 --> 00:17:37.988
<i>Hai, chiizu.</i>[yelps]


00:17:38.162 --> 00:17:39.424
It'’s an ambush!


00:17:39.598 --> 00:17:41.600
You'’ll never take us alive,
foul beasts!


00:17:41.774 --> 00:17:44.125
Calm down, Knuckles.
This is a Chao Garden.


00:17:44.299 --> 00:17:47.389
One of the top ten must-see
spots in all of Tokyo!


00:17:47.563 --> 00:17:49.478
It'’s a perfect place
for us to blend in.


00:17:49.652 --> 00:17:51.306
Are you Detective Pikachu?


00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:52.916
Yes, he is!


00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:56.050
[chortles] He does
look like a Pokémon.


00:17:56.224 --> 00:17:57.181
"Pika, pika!" [laughs]


00:17:57.355 --> 00:17:59.140
Commander Walters!


00:17:59.314 --> 00:18:01.098
Sonic.


00:18:01.272 --> 00:18:04.014
Thank God you'’re all okay.
I'’m sure you have questions.


00:18:04.188 --> 00:18:06.887
Just a big ticked-off
red and black one.


00:18:07.061 --> 00:18:08.453
Who was that guy?


00:18:08.627 --> 00:18:11.326
Shadow'’s story
began a lot like yours, Sonic.


00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.285
But where you found family
and friends on this planet,


00:18:14.459 --> 00:18:17.985
Shadow found only pain and loss.


00:18:18.724 --> 00:18:21.075
<i>It begins over 50 years ago,</i>


00:18:21.249 --> 00:18:24.382
<i>with a meteor crash </i>
<i>in a quiet corner of Oklahoma.</i>


00:18:24.556 --> 00:18:28.169
<i>The meteorite contained</i>
<i>a life-form.</i>


00:18:30.911 --> 00:18:32.695
<i>The ultimate life-form.</i>


00:18:34.697 --> 00:18:37.178
<i>Shadow'’s power--</i>
<i>his "chaos energy"--</i>


00:18:37.352 --> 00:18:40.355
<i>went far beyond</i>
<i>any living creature.</i>


00:18:42.966 --> 00:18:45.534
<i>The scientist</i>
<i>who discovered him</i> <i>believed this power</i>


00:18:45.708 --> 00:18:47.884
<i>would usher in a new era</i>
<i>for humanity.</i>


00:18:49.407 --> 00:18:52.541
<i>But Shadow'’s power</i>
<i>proved too dangerous.</i>


00:18:55.457 --> 00:18:57.459
<i>A terrible accident</i>
<i>destroyed the lab,</i>


00:18:57.633 --> 00:18:59.896
<i>taking human lives with it.</i>[siren wailing]


00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:04.335
<i>The project leader</i>
<i>was blamed for the incident</i> <i>and imprisoned.</i>


00:19:04.509 --> 00:19:06.163
<i>With the program canceled...</i>[yelps in pain]


00:19:06.337 --> 00:19:09.297
<i>...Shadow was a loose end </i>
<i>no one knew how to deal with.</i>


00:19:10.559 --> 00:19:12.474
<i>Too dangerous</i>
<i>to be walking free,</i>


00:19:12.648 --> 00:19:14.998
<i>too valuable to destroy.</i>


00:19:16.086 --> 00:19:18.262
<i>So I had him placed</i>
<i>into stasis...</i>


00:19:20.961 --> 00:19:22.963
<i>indefinitely.</i>


00:19:24.965 --> 00:19:28.055
Wait a second. If Shadow'’s
been on ice for 50 years,


00:19:28.229 --> 00:19:30.492
someone had to help him escape.True.


00:19:30.666 --> 00:19:32.320
But there'’s only a few people
in the world


00:19:32.494 --> 00:19:34.365
who even know
of Shadow'’s existence.


00:19:41.459 --> 00:19:44.332
[J-pop cover of
"I Want You Back" by Jackson 5 playing]


00:19:44.506 --> 00:19:46.682
[people cheering]


00:19:50.468 --> 00:19:52.905
A live show? Yeah!


00:19:56.648 --> 00:19:58.650
[drones humming]


00:20:02.219 --> 00:20:03.220
Get down!


00:20:09.226 --> 00:20:12.403
[people screaming]


00:20:13.578 --> 00:20:15.450
[groaning]


00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:19.193
Egg drones?


00:20:19.367 --> 00:20:22.065
But Robotnik
is supposed to be dead!


00:20:32.858 --> 00:20:35.122
Konnichi-what?


00:20:37.167 --> 00:20:38.386
[weapons powering up]


00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:40.301
[motorbike revving]


00:20:48.918 --> 00:20:50.572
[tires squeal]


00:20:56.056 --> 00:21:00.147
I'’m sorry, we already had
our big motorcycle chase for the evening.


00:21:04.803 --> 00:21:05.761
Commander Walters!


00:21:05.935 --> 00:21:07.197
[Knuckles grunts]


00:21:07.371 --> 00:21:09.417
[Sonic] Commander Walters,
are you okay?


00:21:10.592 --> 00:21:11.593
Sonic...


00:21:11.767 --> 00:21:13.029
[painful grunt]


00:21:14.204 --> 00:21:15.336
...take this.


00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:17.555
[Sonic] What is it?[Walters] A key...


00:21:18.774 --> 00:21:21.342
to the most powerful weapon
GUN has ever built.


00:21:21.516 --> 00:21:24.040
You'’re the only one I trust
to keep it safe.


00:21:24.214 --> 00:21:25.911
[exhales weakly]


00:21:26.086 --> 00:21:27.391
Commander Walters...


00:21:27.565 --> 00:21:29.089
[sirens, vehicles approaching][gasps]


00:21:33.397 --> 00:21:35.051
[indistinct shouts]


00:21:36.226 --> 00:21:37.706
Alpha team, fan out!


00:21:39.099 --> 00:21:40.491
Do we have eyes?


00:21:41.144 --> 00:21:42.145
Secure the perimeter!


00:21:45.453 --> 00:21:46.802
Medevac is en route.


00:21:46.976 --> 00:21:48.630
[indistinct radio chatter]


00:21:50.632 --> 00:21:52.112
His launch key is missing.


00:21:59.336 --> 00:22:01.556
I knew they couldn'’t be trusted.


00:22:03.819 --> 00:22:05.429
[all exclaiming]


00:22:05.603 --> 00:22:07.039
[Tails] Why are we
running from GUN?


00:22:07.214 --> 00:22:08.693
Aren'’t we on the same team?


00:22:08.867 --> 00:22:10.130
[Sonic] Until we get
more information,


00:22:10.304 --> 00:22:12.001
we'’re not trusting anyone.


00:22:12.175 --> 00:22:13.872
Follow me.Get it... off!


00:22:31.586 --> 00:22:33.588
Hold it right there,
Tokyo Drift!


00:22:33.762 --> 00:22:35.155
Who are you?


00:22:38.027 --> 00:22:40.377
[gasps] It'’s the Goat Milker!


00:22:40.551 --> 00:22:42.814
[mimicking Knuckles]
"It'’s the Goat Milker!"


00:22:42.988 --> 00:22:45.034
Relax.
I'’m not here to fight.


00:22:45.208 --> 00:22:48.255
Then why are you here?And why did you free Shadow?


00:22:48.429 --> 00:22:50.344
Are you kidding?


00:22:50.518 --> 00:22:54.130
The last thing we want
is more super-powered hedgehogs running around.


00:22:54.304 --> 00:22:56.263
The doctor had nothing
to do with it.


00:22:57.960 --> 00:22:59.788
And I can prove it.[car alarm chirps]


00:23:15.195 --> 00:23:16.805
Please,


00:23:16.979 --> 00:23:18.023
join me in the crab.


00:23:19.590 --> 00:23:22.767
[narrator] <i>And now back to... </i>
<i>"La UÚltima Pasión."</i>


00:23:22.941 --> 00:23:24.639
I have fallen in love
with another.


00:23:24.813 --> 00:23:26.597
[gasps]


00:23:26.771 --> 00:23:30.035
But who, Gabriella?
Tell me who!


00:23:31.863 --> 00:23:33.996
My twin brother, Pablo?


00:23:35.215 --> 00:23:36.651
<i>Pablo!</i>


00:23:38.566 --> 00:23:39.958
!¡Bastardo!


00:23:40.132 --> 00:23:42.526
Buenos días, !¡hermano!


00:23:42.700 --> 00:23:43.832
<i>No!</i>


00:23:44.006 --> 00:23:46.138
[cackling]


00:23:46.313 --> 00:23:48.619
Let that be a lesson
to you, Juan.


00:23:48.793 --> 00:23:50.360
[beeping]Family


00:23:50.534 --> 00:23:53.755
is a field
of emotional claymores


00:23:53.929 --> 00:23:56.148
that leave you abandoned,
betrayed


00:23:57.933 --> 00:24:00.805
and weeping
while you eat cake,


00:24:00.979 --> 00:24:03.373
which creates copious amounts
of adipose tissue,


00:24:03.547 --> 00:24:06.550
and what some calloused
individuals refer to as...


00:24:06.724 --> 00:24:09.336
[sniffs deeply]
...man boobs.


00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:10.685
Ha.


00:24:12.600 --> 00:24:14.863
[up-tempo Latin jazz playing]


00:24:20.042 --> 00:24:21.652
[slapping along
with the congas]


00:24:24.220 --> 00:24:25.787
[trilling loudly]


00:24:26.918 --> 00:24:28.311
[shrieking]


00:24:28.485 --> 00:24:30.531
Doctor,
we have visitors.


00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:34.012
Really?


00:24:34.186 --> 00:24:36.885
I thought I was having
an anthropomorphic nightmare.


00:24:37.059 --> 00:24:38.539
Where the only person
I could trust in the world


00:24:38.713 --> 00:24:40.236
showed up with
all my worst enemies,


00:24:40.410 --> 00:24:42.107
while I was in a bathrobe,


00:24:42.282 --> 00:24:44.545
playing congas
on my big, fat belly!


00:24:44.719 --> 00:24:45.981
Sorry, sir.


00:24:46.155 --> 00:24:48.288
I don'’t believe it.
Eggman'’s alive?


00:24:48.462 --> 00:24:50.812
And he'’s never
looked worse.


00:24:50.986 --> 00:24:53.293
[cackling] Well, maybe,


00:24:53.467 --> 00:24:57.340
this is what not giving a damn
what you think I look like looks like.


00:24:57.514 --> 00:25:00.735
Sir, right now we have
an even bigger problem.


00:25:00.909 --> 00:25:02.302
Oh, come on.


00:25:04.434 --> 00:25:06.741
There'’s an imposter out there
using your technology.


00:25:06.915 --> 00:25:10.222
Imposter.
That'’s impossi-- What?


00:25:10.397 --> 00:25:11.876
No.


00:25:12.050 --> 00:25:16.098
My sweet mechanized spawn!


00:25:16.272 --> 00:25:19.884
Whomever this party-pooping
posse is looking for


00:25:20.058 --> 00:25:22.365
has stolen my persona


00:25:22.539 --> 00:25:25.890
and the precious babies
from my egg sac.


00:25:26.587 --> 00:25:28.066
Well...


00:25:28.240 --> 00:25:32.636
I'’ll soon egg-xact
my revenge.


00:25:32.810 --> 00:25:34.464
You see what I did there?[chuckles]


00:25:34.638 --> 00:25:37.859
It'’s time for the dramatic
soap-opera twist,


00:25:38.033 --> 00:25:42.167
where this Pablo
reveals his Juan!


00:25:42.342 --> 00:25:46.215
By cross-referencing
the precise coordinates


00:25:46.389 --> 00:25:49.131
of each drone'’s
energy spikes,


00:25:49.871 --> 00:25:52.003
I can track my babies


00:25:52.177 --> 00:25:54.789
to the imposter'’s
base of operations,


00:25:54.963 --> 00:25:56.356
right about...


00:25:56.530 --> 00:25:57.357
there!


00:25:57.531 --> 00:25:59.271
Sonic, I hate to say it,


00:25:59.446 --> 00:26:01.622
but I think we'’re both
after the same person.


00:26:01.796 --> 00:26:04.233
Hold on, hold on.
You'’re not suggesting we team up


00:26:04.407 --> 00:26:06.714
with Doctor Ro-Butt-Stink,
are you?


00:26:06.888 --> 00:26:08.324
Perhaps the fox is right.


00:26:08.498 --> 00:26:11.371
It could be our only chance
to find this mysterious,


00:26:11.545 --> 00:26:12.937
more impressive hedgehog.


00:26:13.111 --> 00:26:14.286
[groans]


00:26:14.461 --> 00:26:16.506
All right, Egghead.
I hate to say it,


00:26:16.680 --> 00:26:18.247
but it looks like
we'’re partners.


00:26:19.379 --> 00:26:21.293
On one condition.


00:26:22.773 --> 00:26:25.341
Dude, you have serious issues.


00:26:25.515 --> 00:26:26.603
Ow!


00:26:28.823 --> 00:26:30.259
[gibbering spasm]


00:26:30.433 --> 00:26:31.608
Let'’s...


00:26:32.392 --> 00:26:33.523
do this!


00:26:33.697 --> 00:26:35.395
["Firestarter"
by The Prodigy playing]


00:26:42.140 --> 00:26:43.272
[pained groan]


00:26:56.807 --> 00:26:58.722
[door thuds][Robotnik grunting]


00:26:59.897 --> 00:27:01.116
Suck it in!


00:27:01.290 --> 00:27:02.465
[grunting][door rattling]


00:27:03.640 --> 00:27:04.989
Tinker-tailor?


00:27:05.163 --> 00:27:06.600
I need room.


00:27:06.774 --> 00:27:09.429
Think Elvis, circa 1976.


00:27:09.603 --> 00:27:11.866
But sir, I don'’t have
the proper materials.


00:27:12.910 --> 00:27:14.259
Found some.


00:27:16.784 --> 00:27:17.959
Resourceful.


00:27:20.396 --> 00:27:22.311
[thunder rumbling]


00:27:45.813 --> 00:27:47.815
[faint, indistinct chatter]


00:27:58.478 --> 00:28:00.567
Hey! This is a restricted area.


00:28:00.741 --> 00:28:03.004
Oh, it'’s okay.
She'’s the professor'’s granddaughter.


00:28:03.178 --> 00:28:05.310
He takes her everywhere.


00:28:05.485 --> 00:28:08.575
Welcome to the lab, Maria.
I'’m Captain Walters.


00:28:08.749 --> 00:28:10.141
Oh, do you know
where my room is?


00:28:10.315 --> 00:28:11.882
Yeah, down the hall
and to the right.


00:28:12.056 --> 00:28:13.580
Make yourself at home.


00:28:13.754 --> 00:28:14.929
But, um,


00:28:15.103 --> 00:28:16.887
let'’s lose the skates,
okay, kiddo?


00:28:17.061 --> 00:28:18.498
Okay.


00:28:23.415 --> 00:28:25.896
[machinery humming softly]


00:28:39.388 --> 00:28:41.521
[fluid bubbling faintly]


00:28:54.882 --> 00:28:56.361
[light chuckle]


00:29:04.326 --> 00:29:05.370
[chuckles]


00:29:06.720 --> 00:29:08.460
[bag rustling]


00:29:10.462 --> 00:29:11.725
[pen uncaps]


00:29:28.176 --> 00:29:29.481
[laughs]


00:29:50.024 --> 00:29:52.896
["End of the Line"
by the Traveling Wilburys playing]


00:30:18.095 --> 00:30:19.270
[delighted shriek]


00:30:19.444 --> 00:30:21.272
[squealing]


00:30:28.976 --> 00:30:29.803
[gasps]


00:30:29.977 --> 00:30:30.934
[yelling]


00:30:35.722 --> 00:30:36.897
[whooping]


00:30:38.725 --> 00:30:39.900
Look out!


00:30:41.466 --> 00:30:42.642
[crashing]


00:30:59.136 --> 00:31:00.572
[faint roaring]


00:31:18.286 --> 00:31:20.462
[song ends]


00:31:20.636 --> 00:31:22.725
[crickets chirping softly]


00:31:23.813 --> 00:31:24.988
Wow.


00:31:25.685 --> 00:31:27.121
Look at all those stars.


00:31:28.949 --> 00:31:30.777
They'’re like diamonds.


00:31:32.474 --> 00:31:34.215
My grandfather says


00:31:34.389 --> 00:31:36.043
it can take hundreds of years


00:31:36.217 --> 00:31:38.219
for the light of a star
to reach Earth.


00:31:38.959 --> 00:31:40.830
And by the time you see it,


00:31:41.004 --> 00:31:43.311
the star might not even
exist anymore.


00:31:44.834 --> 00:31:46.314
Isn'’t that crazy?


00:31:47.794 --> 00:31:49.665
A light shines,


00:31:49.839 --> 00:31:51.798
even though the star is gone.


00:31:53.364 --> 00:31:55.192
Yeah, it does.


00:31:57.020 --> 00:31:58.718
I wonder which one
you came from, Shadow.


00:31:58.892 --> 00:31:59.762
I don'’t know.


00:32:00.894 --> 00:32:03.374
I don'’t know anything
about my home.


00:32:03.548 --> 00:32:05.942
This is your home, Shadow.


00:32:06.682 --> 00:32:07.814
Earth.


00:32:14.734 --> 00:32:16.039
Maria,


00:32:16.692 --> 00:32:18.389
do you think I'’m...


00:32:19.347 --> 00:32:20.609
dangerous?


00:32:21.871 --> 00:32:23.699
What are you talking about?


00:32:23.873 --> 00:32:26.441
The way the scientists
look at me,


00:32:26.615 --> 00:32:28.312
I can tell they'’re afraid.


00:32:28.486 --> 00:32:32.055
Like I'’m the horrible thing
from that movie we watched.


00:32:33.143 --> 00:32:34.579
I don'’t know...


00:32:35.276 --> 00:32:36.756
what I am.


00:32:42.022 --> 00:32:43.588
You'’re my friend.


00:32:44.938 --> 00:32:47.592
And you can do or be
anything you want.


00:32:48.768 --> 00:32:50.378
Not because of your powers,


00:32:50.552 --> 00:32:53.990
but because of who you are...
in here.


00:32:56.819 --> 00:32:58.995
I don'’t know what I'’d do
without you.


00:33:08.788 --> 00:33:11.791
["End of the Line" resumes]


00:33:16.273 --> 00:33:17.971
[song ends abruptly]


00:33:18.145 --> 00:33:19.799
[dust crackling]


00:33:36.641 --> 00:33:38.252
[footfalls]


00:33:40.907 --> 00:33:42.604
Professor?


00:33:42.778 --> 00:33:45.825
It'’s good to see you,
Shadow.


00:33:45.999 --> 00:33:48.088
I knew you'’d come home.


00:33:48.262 --> 00:33:50.830
I can'’t get her out of my head.


00:33:51.004 --> 00:33:52.527
The pain...


00:33:52.701 --> 00:33:54.050
It'’s too much.


00:33:54.224 --> 00:33:57.706
And that is why
we have to punish them.


00:34:02.232 --> 00:34:03.843
Okay, I don'’t like you
and you don'’t like me.


00:34:04.017 --> 00:34:05.845
Let'’s get this
over with quickly.


00:34:06.019 --> 00:34:07.847
Out of my way, dorkupine.


00:34:08.021 --> 00:34:10.110
"Dorkupine"?
Really clever.


00:34:14.549 --> 00:34:16.420
[hollow tapping]


00:34:16.594 --> 00:34:18.683
This door is six-inch-thick
solid steel


00:34:18.858 --> 00:34:20.642
on a pressurized latch.


00:34:20.816 --> 00:34:22.992
I'’ll need a moment to calculate
the molecular density


00:34:23.166 --> 00:34:24.776
and invert
the venting mechanics.


00:34:24.951 --> 00:34:26.387
[thunderous crash]


00:34:28.432 --> 00:34:29.694
[Knuckles] I unlocked it.


00:34:29.869 --> 00:34:32.872
[Robotnik] Subtle as always,
fist-for-brains.


00:34:34.134 --> 00:34:35.875
Easy, Shadow.


00:34:36.049 --> 00:34:38.529
Those are the guests
I'’ve been expecting.


00:34:38.703 --> 00:34:41.358
Let'’s give them
a warm welcome.


00:34:45.188 --> 00:34:46.537
[Stone] Whoa.


00:34:46.711 --> 00:34:47.974
What is this place?


00:34:48.148 --> 00:34:50.106
[Sonic] It looks like
a military base,


00:34:50.280 --> 00:34:52.108
but nobody'’s been here
for years.


00:34:52.282 --> 00:34:53.675
I wonder if it'’s haunted.


00:34:53.849 --> 00:34:56.765
Haunted? Nobody said anything
about being haunted.


00:34:56.939 --> 00:34:59.899
What'’s the matter?
You afraid of g-g-g-ghosts?


00:35:00.073 --> 00:35:02.162
Nothing scares
an Echidna warrior.


00:35:02.336 --> 00:35:04.729
Uh, yeah. Do you remember
what happened last movie night?


00:35:04.904 --> 00:35:06.470
[screaming in terror]


00:35:06.644 --> 00:35:07.950
[piercing scream][all yelling]


00:35:08.124 --> 00:35:09.560
Let go, let go, let go!


00:35:09.734 --> 00:35:12.433
There is no such thing
as a friendly ghost.


00:35:14.000 --> 00:35:15.523
[Sonic]
So which way do we go?


00:35:15.697 --> 00:35:19.396
I know! We should split up.


00:35:19.570 --> 00:35:22.791
Everyone with hideous,
brightly-colored fur take the left and the middle.


00:35:22.965 --> 00:35:24.575
Stone and I will go right.


00:35:24.749 --> 00:35:26.490
No, no, no, no, no. I'’m not
letting you out of my sight.


00:35:26.664 --> 00:35:28.449
Tails, you and Stone go left.


00:35:28.623 --> 00:35:31.713
Knuckles, you take the middle.
Eggman, you and me go right.


00:35:31.887 --> 00:35:33.802
By all means.


00:35:33.976 --> 00:35:35.456
We could use some
time together.


00:35:35.630 --> 00:35:37.240
To work on
your trust issues.


00:35:37.414 --> 00:35:40.243
You know what? You'’re right.
I should be more trusting.


00:35:40.417 --> 00:35:43.203
I mean, you'’ve only tried
to kill me twice!


00:35:45.248 --> 00:35:47.468
Just a dark, creepy hallway.


00:35:47.642 --> 00:35:49.339
Nothing to be afraid of.


00:35:51.080 --> 00:35:52.777
You hear that, ghost?


00:35:52.952 --> 00:35:54.475
You don'’t frighten me!


00:35:54.649 --> 00:35:56.216
[steam hissing][yells]


00:35:58.958 --> 00:36:01.351
Get... a... grip.


00:36:02.265 --> 00:36:04.006
Boo.[screams]


00:36:06.704 --> 00:36:09.403
I'’m just gonna
come right out and say this:


00:36:09.577 --> 00:36:12.362
You'’re adorable.[chuckles]
Oh, um, thanks.


00:36:12.536 --> 00:36:15.975
So, what'’s it like
being Sonic'’s assistant?


00:36:16.149 --> 00:36:19.456
You have a daily routine?
Paid time off? Benefits?


00:36:19.630 --> 00:36:22.807
Oh, I'’m not Sonic'’s assistant.
We'’re teammates.


00:36:22.982 --> 00:36:24.984
He'’s the leader,
Knuckles is the muscle,


00:36:25.158 --> 00:36:26.724
and I'’m the gadget guy.


00:36:26.898 --> 00:36:28.248
We all have a role to play.


00:36:28.422 --> 00:36:30.163
That'’s what makes the team
so special!


00:36:30.337 --> 00:36:32.078
That and the fact
we'’re best friends.


00:36:32.817 --> 00:36:34.123
You are?


00:36:34.297 --> 00:36:36.125
Well, yeah.
Just like you and Eggman, right?


00:36:37.953 --> 00:36:39.999
Uh... Yeah, eh...


00:36:40.173 --> 00:36:42.175
Of course! Yes.


00:36:42.349 --> 00:36:45.221
Me and the doctor,
best of friends.


00:36:46.701 --> 00:36:48.268
That'’s definitely
what we are.


00:36:48.442 --> 00:36:50.574
[metallic clattering]


00:36:50.748 --> 00:36:52.533
[squeaking]


00:36:53.490 --> 00:36:54.535
Hmm.


00:36:59.540 --> 00:37:01.281
[both screaming]


00:37:13.641 --> 00:37:17.210
Whoa. Look at all this stuff.


00:37:17.384 --> 00:37:20.517
This was more than
just a military base or a lab.


00:37:21.083 --> 00:37:22.519
It was a home.


00:37:22.693 --> 00:37:24.260
People lived here.


00:37:24.869 --> 00:37:26.349
He had a family.


00:37:27.089 --> 00:37:28.917
Is that what I smell?


00:37:29.091 --> 00:37:32.181
The stench
of domestic harmony?


00:37:32.355 --> 00:37:35.880
You ever wonder what
your life would have been like if you had a family?


00:37:36.055 --> 00:37:37.491
Hmm... No!


00:37:37.665 --> 00:37:39.667
Maybe you wouldn'’t have gone
full supervillain.


00:37:39.841 --> 00:37:42.670
I have no parents,
no aunts, no uncles.


00:37:42.844 --> 00:37:45.368
And something about my attitude
renders me...


00:37:46.326 --> 00:37:50.460
undesirable
to all possible genders.


00:37:52.332 --> 00:37:54.508
My future is a cul-de-sac!


00:37:55.509 --> 00:37:57.511
The Robotnik name ends...


00:37:59.165 --> 00:38:00.818
<i>avec moi.</i>


00:38:00.992 --> 00:38:03.038
Yes, I know French.


00:38:04.083 --> 00:38:05.562
[shuddering spasm]


00:38:07.564 --> 00:38:08.652
Whoa.


00:38:08.826 --> 00:38:11.829
Is this where you grew up,
Shadow?


00:38:12.003 --> 00:38:13.788
No wonder you'’re so mad.


00:38:13.962 --> 00:38:16.834
This place could really use
a beanbag chair


00:38:17.008 --> 00:38:18.314
and some comic books.


00:38:19.837 --> 00:38:21.056
What happened here?


00:38:21.752 --> 00:38:22.927
[hard grunt]


00:38:23.102 --> 00:38:25.234
I'’m tired
of giving you warnings!


00:38:26.105 --> 00:38:28.107
[grunts, yells]


00:38:29.108 --> 00:38:30.500
Where'’d you go, hedgehog?


00:38:30.674 --> 00:38:32.546
I wasn'’t finished
trauma dumping.


00:38:34.374 --> 00:38:37.159
My darlings!


00:38:37.333 --> 00:38:38.856
[inhales, giggles]


00:38:39.030 --> 00:38:41.468
My eggy weggies!


00:38:42.599 --> 00:38:45.646
[professor] ♪ <i>Memories</i>♪


00:38:45.820 --> 00:38:49.171
♪ <i>Light the corners</i>♪


00:38:49.345 --> 00:38:53.001
♪ <i>Of my mind</i>♪


00:38:53.175 --> 00:38:56.309
♪ <i>Misty watercolor</i>♪


00:38:56.483 --> 00:39:02.097
♪ <i>Memories</i>♪


00:39:02.271 --> 00:39:05.144
♪ <i>Of the way</i>♪


00:39:05.318 --> 00:39:10.584
♪ <i>We weren'’t</i>♪


00:39:11.541 --> 00:39:12.542
I...


00:39:14.283 --> 00:39:16.024
don'’t believe it.Don'’t you?


00:39:16.198 --> 00:39:17.460
It'’s impossible.Is it?


00:39:17.634 --> 00:39:18.548
It couldn'’t be.Couldn'’t it?


00:39:18.722 --> 00:39:19.506
I'’m--Are you?


00:39:19.680 --> 00:39:20.855
Imposter!


00:39:21.029 --> 00:39:23.292
You stole my babies!


00:39:23.466 --> 00:39:26.643
But they know
who their real daddy is...


00:39:26.817 --> 00:39:27.905
drone-napper!


00:39:28.079 --> 00:39:29.603
[chortling]


00:39:29.777 --> 00:39:32.867
Magnificent creations,
my boy.


00:39:33.041 --> 00:39:35.609
I borrowed them
to lure you here


00:39:35.783 --> 00:39:37.785
and reunite our family.


00:39:39.526 --> 00:39:41.180
You see, Ivo...


00:39:43.312 --> 00:39:46.315
I'’m your grandfather:


00:39:46.489 --> 00:39:48.926
Gerald Robotnik.


00:39:52.974 --> 00:39:55.672
My... grandfather?


00:39:57.413 --> 00:40:00.286
But how? And why?


00:40:01.069 --> 00:40:03.114
And who did what with whom?


00:40:03.289 --> 00:40:08.207
You hail from an ancestry
of excellence...


00:40:08.381 --> 00:40:10.948
tied directly <i>à moi.</i>


00:40:11.122 --> 00:40:14.038
Yes, I know French.


00:40:16.563 --> 00:40:18.086
You do look like me.


00:40:19.043 --> 00:40:21.002
But fatter. And older.


00:40:21.872 --> 00:40:23.831
And there'’s that funny smell.


00:40:25.528 --> 00:40:28.357
But the resemblance
is uncanny.


00:40:29.228 --> 00:40:30.838
It'’s as if...


00:40:31.012 --> 00:40:33.101
[both]
...we'’re two characters in a movie


00:40:33.275 --> 00:40:35.843
being played
by the same actor.


00:40:36.017 --> 00:40:38.454
But I need real proof!Ivo!


00:40:38.628 --> 00:40:39.934
We have very little time.


00:40:41.457 --> 00:40:43.590
But I could field
a couple of queries.


00:40:43.764 --> 00:40:46.897
Name the most elegant formula
in mathematics.


00:40:47.071 --> 00:40:48.421
Euler'’s Identity.


00:40:48.595 --> 00:40:50.901
E to the I times pi plus one
equals zilch.


00:40:51.075 --> 00:40:52.903
European capitals
arranged alphabetically


00:40:53.077 --> 00:40:54.340
by the fourth letter.


00:40:54.514 --> 00:40:56.255
Riga, Monaco, Sarajevo, Tirana.


00:40:56.429 --> 00:40:58.213
The speed of light
divided by the speed of sound,


00:40:58.387 --> 00:41:00.433
divided by
the speed of the bus in the movie <i>Speed.</i>


00:41:00.607 --> 00:41:01.956
[mimics adding machine]


00:41:02.130 --> 00:41:04.698
17,893.33333...


00:41:04.872 --> 00:41:08.310
Rounding up?17,894 MPH.


00:41:08.484 --> 00:41:10.965
And, for all the marbles...


00:41:11.139 --> 00:41:13.315
Good. I lost mine.


00:41:13.489 --> 00:41:15.535
A rare lung disease,


00:41:15.709 --> 00:41:18.799
and the longest word
in the English dictionary.


00:41:19.452 --> 00:41:20.931
Um...


00:41:21.105 --> 00:41:24.413
[both] Pneumonoultramicroscopic-
silicovolcanoconiosis!


00:41:25.284 --> 00:41:28.939
Pap-pap!In the saggy flesh.


00:41:29.113 --> 00:41:31.202
But looking pretty good
for a hundred and ten.


00:41:31.377 --> 00:41:32.943
[shuddering grunt]


00:41:33.640 --> 00:41:36.251
Oh, Grampy-poo! [laughs]


00:41:39.646 --> 00:41:43.432
Where have you been
my entire life?


00:41:43.606 --> 00:41:45.173
[moans happily]


00:41:45.347 --> 00:41:47.349
[gasps] Wait.


00:41:47.523 --> 00:41:49.743
Where have you been...
my entire life?


00:41:49.917 --> 00:41:55.923
Locked in
a top-secret prison for the last 50 years.


00:41:56.097 --> 00:41:59.361
Made it kind of hard
to send Christmas cards.


00:41:59.535 --> 00:42:01.015
Now...


00:42:01.189 --> 00:42:04.758
you'’re probably wondering
why I brought you here.


00:42:04.932 --> 00:42:06.325
You didn'’t bring me here!


00:42:06.499 --> 00:42:09.806
I used my unparalleled intellect
to track you down.


00:42:09.980 --> 00:42:13.897
Per the plan
I concocted with my unparalleled intellect.


00:42:14.071 --> 00:42:15.856
You'’ll see.


00:42:16.030 --> 00:42:18.598
I have the answer
to everything.


00:42:20.208 --> 00:42:21.862
Come on, kiddo.


00:42:30.261 --> 00:42:32.655
[groaning]


00:42:35.658 --> 00:42:37.617
Oh, no. Oh, no, no.


00:42:37.791 --> 00:42:39.619
Someone tell me
this is some kind of


00:42:39.793 --> 00:42:41.925
concussion-induced nightmare.


00:42:42.099 --> 00:42:44.232
There'’s two Eggmen now?


00:42:44.406 --> 00:42:46.408
Double your villains,
double your fun!


00:42:46.582 --> 00:42:49.368
Two Robotniks
are way worse than one.


00:42:49.542 --> 00:42:50.543
Chest bump?


00:42:50.717 --> 00:42:51.544
No.


00:42:52.632 --> 00:42:54.721
Stone,
why are you tied up?


00:42:54.895 --> 00:42:57.463
Do that on your own time.
You sicken me.


00:42:57.637 --> 00:43:00.030
You must be
the long-lost grandson.


00:43:00.204 --> 00:43:03.077
And you must be
another stinking hedgehog.


00:43:03.251 --> 00:43:05.296
So you'’re the one
behind all this.


00:43:05.471 --> 00:43:07.690
The Shadow breakout.The attack on Walters.


00:43:07.864 --> 00:43:09.039
That musty
old-man smell.


00:43:09.213 --> 00:43:11.172
How dare you insult me


00:43:11.346 --> 00:43:13.000
with your unsolicited
exposition!


00:43:13.174 --> 00:43:15.263
Shadow, get the key.


00:43:15.437 --> 00:43:16.438
Where is it?


00:43:16.612 --> 00:43:18.701
Ha! Good one, Hot Topic.


00:43:18.875 --> 00:43:20.964
Do you really think
we'’d be that stupid


00:43:21.138 --> 00:43:23.184
to bring the key
right to you?


00:43:23.358 --> 00:43:24.794
Yep, we'’re that stupid.


00:43:24.968 --> 00:43:27.144
GUN took everything from us.


00:43:27.318 --> 00:43:30.234
And now we are going
to take everything from them.


00:43:30.409 --> 00:43:31.671
[Gerald] With this.


00:43:31.845 --> 00:43:35.501
My masterpiece
of malevolence...


00:43:35.675 --> 00:43:38.199
The Eclipse Cannon.


00:43:38.373 --> 00:43:41.463
<i>In exchange</i>
<i>for my freedom,</i>


00:43:41.637 --> 00:43:43.770
<i>I gave GUN</i>
<i>the most powerful weapon</i>


00:43:43.944 --> 00:43:46.468
<i>mankind has ever seen,</i>


00:43:46.642 --> 00:43:49.210
<i>capable of delivering</i>
<i>a precision strike</i>


00:43:49.384 --> 00:43:50.777
<i>anywhere on Earth.</i>


00:43:52.213 --> 00:43:53.432
<i>Our first target:</i>


00:43:54.258 --> 00:43:55.912
<i>GUN Headquarters.</i>


00:43:56.086 --> 00:43:58.219
But firing a weapon
that powerful


00:43:58.393 --> 00:44:00.351
could threaten millions
of innocent lives!


00:44:00.526 --> 00:44:02.789
Yeah, tera-bite me.[cackles]


00:44:02.963 --> 00:44:07.837
This is one of two keys required
to launch the Eclipse Cannon.


00:44:08.011 --> 00:44:10.318
The other is locked
inside GUN headquarters.


00:44:10.492 --> 00:44:12.363
Once we have both,


00:44:12.538 --> 00:44:15.366
I will take rightful control
of my weapon.


00:44:15.541 --> 00:44:17.325
I'’m in.


00:44:24.288 --> 00:44:25.768
Holy crab!


00:44:25.942 --> 00:44:27.553
[Robotnik]
Spacious and crustaceous.


00:44:28.467 --> 00:44:29.642
Thank you so much


00:44:29.816 --> 00:44:31.470
for inspiring
this little adventure.


00:44:31.644 --> 00:44:33.820
It really worked out
for me.


00:44:33.994 --> 00:44:36.953
And you wonder why
I have trust issues!


00:44:38.433 --> 00:44:40.609
Shadow, wait! Don'’t do this.


00:44:40.783 --> 00:44:42.176
I know you'’re hurting,


00:44:42.350 --> 00:44:44.874
but don'’t let that change
who you are inside.


00:44:45.048 --> 00:44:49.313
I'’ve spent 50 years
reliving what they did to her.


00:44:49.488 --> 00:44:52.403
This is who I am inside.


00:44:58.409 --> 00:45:02.457
Uh, nice magic marble.
Real scary.


00:45:05.678 --> 00:45:07.680
[yelps] That actually
is real scary!


00:45:09.769 --> 00:45:11.248
It'’s a mini black hole!


00:45:11.422 --> 00:45:13.773
It'’s going to suck in
all the matter in this base!


00:45:17.341 --> 00:45:18.865
[all yelling]


00:45:19.039 --> 00:45:20.954
Fear not, friends.


00:45:21.650 --> 00:45:23.522
Even my teeth are muscles!


00:45:24.174 --> 00:45:25.132
[Sonic yelps]


00:45:25.306 --> 00:45:26.829
[Knuckles growls]


00:45:29.092 --> 00:45:31.573
Sonic, try to reach
one of my rings!


00:45:31.747 --> 00:45:32.966
[Sonic] Got one.


00:45:33.140 --> 00:45:35.359
Check this out. Trick shot!


00:45:35.534 --> 00:45:36.752
[grunts]


00:45:39.059 --> 00:45:40.539
Come on.


00:45:41.801 --> 00:45:43.367
Come on.


00:45:43.542 --> 00:45:45.195
Come on.[Knuckles groans]


00:45:46.806 --> 00:45:48.503
[both] Come on!


00:45:49.243 --> 00:45:50.157
[yells]


00:45:50.331 --> 00:45:52.507
[all yelling]


00:45:57.904 --> 00:46:00.428
Yeah! Yes!


00:46:04.127 --> 00:46:05.128
[Sonic] Yikes.


00:46:06.434 --> 00:46:08.218
Somebody better call
Google Maps.


00:46:09.393 --> 00:46:11.961
[rumbling faintly]


00:46:12.135 --> 00:46:16.270
I'’ve spent years
trying to cleanse the cosmos


00:46:16.444 --> 00:46:20.100
of that spiny,
blue speed freak.


00:46:20.274 --> 00:46:21.928
And you did it...


00:46:23.451 --> 00:46:25.279
in one afternoon.


00:46:25.453 --> 00:46:29.370
There'’s nothing
we can'’t destroy together, my boy.


00:46:29.544 --> 00:46:32.416
Charting route to GUN
Headquarters in London, sirs.


00:46:32.591 --> 00:46:34.680
ETA four hours.


00:46:34.854 --> 00:46:36.159
As the crab flies.


00:46:36.333 --> 00:46:38.684
By all accounts,
we'’re ahead of schedule.


00:46:39.641 --> 00:46:41.556
We should take this time


00:46:41.730 --> 00:46:43.732
to get to know
each other better.


00:46:43.906 --> 00:46:45.647
Wow. What?


00:46:46.387 --> 00:46:47.475
You mean...


00:46:47.649 --> 00:46:50.913
spend some
qua-qua-quality time?


00:46:51.087 --> 00:46:55.831
You'’ve waited for this
your whole life.


00:46:56.005 --> 00:47:02.316
How would you choose
to spend one perfect day with your new grand pal?


00:47:14.154 --> 00:47:15.459
[elbow thuds][grunts]


00:47:16.373 --> 00:47:17.897
[both screaming]


00:47:18.071 --> 00:47:19.899
["Wouldn'’t It Be Nice"
by the Beach Boys playing]


00:47:20.639 --> 00:47:21.944
[bell dinging]


00:47:25.382 --> 00:47:26.166
[yelps]


00:47:26.340 --> 00:47:27.297
[wincing groan]


00:47:46.577 --> 00:47:47.535
[shrieks happily]


00:47:56.196 --> 00:47:59.503
Ooh! [chortling]


00:47:59.678 --> 00:48:02.419
[rockets whistle and explode]


00:48:13.735 --> 00:48:15.519
[song fades out]


00:48:17.217 --> 00:48:20.220
[song resumes]


00:48:27.314 --> 00:48:28.794
[song ends]


00:48:38.325 --> 00:48:39.761
And done!


00:48:39.935 --> 00:48:42.677
Masterpiece.
Look at that.Yay!


00:48:42.851 --> 00:48:46.289
It'’s really been great
having time to ourselves.


00:48:46.463 --> 00:48:48.901
Right. Absolutely.
I just feel so...


00:48:49.075 --> 00:48:50.467
relaxed, you know?
Clearheaded.


00:48:50.641 --> 00:48:52.948
Mmm, look at all these
new interests we found.


00:48:53.122 --> 00:48:55.124
I know, so many hobbies.So many!


00:48:55.298 --> 00:48:58.127
After the action and adventure
of the last few years,


00:48:58.301 --> 00:49:00.521
well, I could get used to this.Same.


00:49:00.695 --> 00:49:02.697
[deep rumbling]


00:49:06.266 --> 00:49:08.616
[Sonic] Tom! Maddie!
We need your help on a super--


00:49:08.790 --> 00:49:11.619
Knuckles, do you mind?Oh! Excuse me.


00:49:11.793 --> 00:49:13.229
Tom! Maddie! We need your help


00:49:13.403 --> 00:49:14.927
on a super-dangerous
top-secret mission!


00:49:15.101 --> 00:49:16.145
Hmm.


00:49:17.886 --> 00:49:19.540
Thank God. Yeah, we'’re in.Let'’s go.


00:49:19.714 --> 00:49:21.934
Really? You'’re in?
Just like that?


00:49:22.108 --> 00:49:24.850
Yes. It was getting so boring
without you guys here.Yeah. So...


00:49:25.024 --> 00:49:26.677
No offense....boring. No, none taken.


00:49:26.852 --> 00:49:28.331
I mean, whatever crazy plan
you'’re cooking up,


00:49:28.505 --> 00:49:29.811
the answer'’s yes.Yes.


00:49:29.985 --> 00:49:32.945
Great. But first things first:
What is that?


00:49:33.119 --> 00:49:34.598
Oh! This is...


00:49:34.773 --> 00:49:36.209
[in puppet voice]
...Li'’l Tom!


00:49:36.383 --> 00:49:37.863
[normal voice]
Isn'’t he great?


00:49:39.429 --> 00:49:41.649
I told you
to get rid of that. It'’s very creepy.


00:49:41.823 --> 00:49:42.998
[puppet voice]
I told him to get rid of you.


00:49:43.172 --> 00:49:44.565
